<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105078" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐοδ-ίτης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑτ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who frequents cross-roads</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριοδίτας: τοὺς ἐν τῇ τριόδῳ
				διαλοιδορουμένους,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				309
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριοδίτης τριπύλιος,</span>
			title of Menippean Satire by Varro, Non.<i><span class="en">
				p.306L.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριοδῖτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, ἡ, epith. of
			Hecate, <i>who was worshipped at the meeting of three ways,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Chariclid.
				1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> epith. of
			the Moon, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.937f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Doroth.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				2.82
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοβὰς τ.</span>”
				<i>street-walker,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.568
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> generally,
				<i>common, vulgar,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μοῦσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tz.
					<u>H.</u>
					12.513
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> name of <i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>, Anatol. ap.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				37
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
